📒 Basic Contact Book

Welcome to the Basic Contact Book project! 📱✨ This is a simple console-based application designed to store and manage contact information efficiently. The program allows users to add, view, search, update, and delete contacts through an easy-to-use menu system. 🧑‍💻

🎯 Project Objective

The main objective of this project is to create a basic Contact Book using programming fundamentals such as variables, dictionaries, functions, loops, conditional statements, and user input. It is a beginner-friendly project that demonstrates how data can be stored and managed inside a Python program. 🐍

🛠️ Technologies Used

🐍 Programming Language: Python
💻 Interface: Console / Terminal
📦 Libraries: No external libraries required

🚀 How the Program Works

1️⃣ Create the Contact Book

First, an empty dictionary is created to store the contacts. A dictionary is useful because each contact can have a unique name as its key, while the corresponding phone number can be stored as its value.

contacts = {}

The "{}" syntax creates an empty dictionary.

2️⃣ Display the Menu

The program displays a menu containing different operations such as adding, viewing, searching, updating, and deleting contacts.

print("1. Add Contact")
print("2. View Contacts")
print("3. Search Contact")
print("4. Update Contact")
print("5. Delete Contact")
print("6. Exit")

The "print()" function is used to display information on the screen.

3️⃣ Add a Contact ➕

The user is asked to enter a contact name and phone number. The information is then stored in the dictionary.

name = input("Enter contact name: ")
phone = input("Enter phone number: ")

contacts[name] = phone

The "input()" function is used to receive information from the user. Dictionary assignment using "contacts[name] = phone" stores the contact.

4️⃣ View All Contacts 👀

The program can display all contacts stored in the Contact Book.

for name, phone in contacts.items():
    print(name, ":", phone)

The "for" loop is used to iterate through the contacts, while the ".items()" dictionary method returns both the key and value.

5️⃣ Search for a Contact 🔍

The user can search for a specific contact by entering the contact name.

name = input("Enter name to search: ")

if name in contacts:
    print("Phone:", contacts[name])
else:
    print("Contact not found.")

The "in" operator checks whether the entered name exists in the dictionary. The "if-else" statement is used to display the appropriate result.

6️⃣ Update a Contact ✏️

Existing contact information can be changed by entering the contact name and a new phone number.

name = input("Enter contact name: ")

if name in contacts:
    phone = input("Enter new phone number: ")
    contacts[name] = phone
    print("Contact updated successfully.")
else:
    print("Contact not found.")

The existing dictionary value is replaced with the new phone number.

7️⃣ Delete a Contact 🗑️

A contact can be removed from the Contact Book using the "del" statement.

name = input("Enter contact name: ")

if name in contacts:
    del contacts[name]
    print("Contact deleted successfully.")
else:
    print("Contact not found.")

The "del" statement removes the specified contact from the dictionary.

8️⃣ Exit the Program 🚪

The program provides an option to exit. A "while" loop can be used to keep the menu running until the user selects the exit option.

while True:
    # Menu operations

    if choice == "6":
        break

The "while True" statement continuously executes the program, and the "break" statement terminates the loop when the user chooses to exit.

